  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n\u00ac(A\u2227B)=\u00acA\u2228\u00acB\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\u00ac(P\\text{\u00a0is not a rhombus}\\text{\u00a0and\u00a0}Q\\text{\u00a0is not a rectangle}) & \u2261\u00ac((P\\text{\u00a0is not a rhombus})\u2227(Q\\text{\u00a0is not a rectangle})) \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac(P\\text{\u00a0is not a rhombus})\u2228\u00ac(Q\\text{\u00a0is not a rectangle}) \\\\  & \u2261(P\\text{\u00a0is a rhombus})\u2228(Q\\text{\u00a0is a rectangle}) \\\\  & \u2261P\\text{\u00a0is a rhombus}\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}Q\\text{\u00a0is a rectangle}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
